Task prompt: You're building a modular spaceship! Implement the `Spaceship` class to use composition. It should take an `engine` and a `weaponSystem` in its constructor and delegate its `activateThrusters` and `engageWeapons` actions to these components.

Current code in the editor:
```
class Engine {
  constructor(thrust) {
    this.thrust = thrust;
  }
  start() {
    return `Engine firing with ${this.thrust} kN of thrust!`;
  }
}

class WeaponSystem {
  constructor(damage) {
    this.damage = damage;
  }
  fire() {
    return `Weapons engaged, inflicting ${this.damage} damage!`;
  }
}

class Spaceship {
  // TODO: Add constructor to take engine and weaponSystem
  constructor(engine, weaponSystem) {
    this.engine = engine; // TODO: Assign engine
    this.weaponSystem = weaponSystem; // TODO: Assign weaponSystem
  }

  activateThrusters() {
    // TODO: Delegate to the engine's start method
    return this.engine.start();
  }

  engageWeapons() {
    // TODO: Delegate to the weaponSystem's fire method
    return this.weaponSystem.fire();
  }
}

// Example usage:
const impulseEngine = new Engine(5000);
const laserCannons = new WeaponSystem(120);
const starship = new Spaceship(impulseEngine, laserCannons);

console.log(starship.activateThrusters());
console.log(starship.engageWeapons());
```

